# Test: the built le binary answers the RFC extraction envelope, the
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
# conformance check, the audit re-seal and the requirement ledger. Every action
# the rfc listing names and every supported rendering are exercised through the
# developer-facing binary; the writers run against isolated exports of HEAD.
#
# The check is judged on its CONTRACT and never on this checkout's violation
# count. It has three answers -- clean, violations, and a tree it could not read
# -- and each is driven from a tree the fixture owns. The discriminating case
# seeds ONE gated MUST that no test tags into an export of HEAD and requires the
# gate to name that requirement and exit 2, because a count read off the shared
# checkout is met by whatever backlog is standing that day.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-le-is-a-ze-binary AC-1, AC-7, AC-8 and AC-11 over the real
# tree and the artifact a developer runs.
#
# The timeout is declared because a cold build cache and the RFC tree walks are
# substantially slower than steady-state execution.

option=timeout:value=900s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture ui/le-rfc-answers
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
